# Hand-made requests for the demos. Open in IntelliJ / WebStorm (built-in HTTP client) or VS Code
# (REST Client extension) and click the ▶ next to a request. Same thing as curl, minus the quoting.

@host = http://localhost:4000

### Browse
GET {{host}}/api/products

### One product (the gateway asks catalog, catalog asks its database)
GET {{host}}/api/products/p1

### Place an order: 2 keyboards. Watch ONE trace span gateway → orders → catalog → inventory → payments → notifications
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customer": "demo@example.com", "items": [{ "productId": "p1", "quantity": 2 }] }

### THE PRODUCTION BUG: 5 monitor stands → HTTP 500 (demo 2 explains why)
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customer": "demo@example.com", "items": [{ "productId": "p3", "quantity": 5 }] }

### 5 keyboards works (this product HAS a bulk discount)
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customer": "demo@example.com", "items": [{ "productId": "p1", "quantity": 5 }] }

### The CPU-heavy revenue report: ~120ms with nothing to wait for. Fire it a few times while an order runs.
GET {{host}}/api/orders/summary

### BEFORE / AFTER pairs (demo 3)
GET {{host}}/api/orders/recent/n-plus-one

###
GET {{host}}/api/orders/recent/batched

###
GET {{host}}/api/products/p1/recommendations/uncached

###
GET {{host}}/api/products/p1/recommendations/cached

###
GET {{host}}/api/dashboard/sequential

###
GET {{host}}/api/dashboard/parallel
